   "tag": "p×2",
   "class": "wp-block-paragraph",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 272,
   "text": "There was no spec for this property for quite a while, but now is covered under CSS Basic User Interface Module Level 4.\nThe default value is auto, which makes selection happen normally as you expect. “Normally” is a bit complicated. It’s worth quoting from the spec here:",
   "counts": {
    "links": 1,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 0,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 2,
    "repeats": 2,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.14,
   "geometry": {
    "top": 1843,
    "height": 192,
    "widthFraction": 0.43,
    "leftFraction": 0.21,
    "pageFraction": 0.12,
    "aboveFold": false
   }
  },
  {
   "index": 9,
   "tag": "blockquote",
   "class": "wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 404,
   "text": "On the ::before and ::after pseudo elements, the computed value is none\nIf the element is an editable element, the computed value is contain\nOtherwise, if the computed value of user-select on the parent of this element is all, the computed value is all\nOtherwise, if the computed value of user-select on the parent of this element is none, the computed value is none\nOtherwise, the computed value is ",
   "counts": {
    "links": 2,
    "images": 0,
    "headings": 0,
    "listItems": 5,
    "tableRows": 0,
    "controls": 0,
    "paragraphs": 0,
    "repeats": 1,
    "coverLinks": 0
   },
   "linkTextRatio": 0.04,
