   "tag": "p×2",
   "class": "wp-block-paragraph",
   "landmarks": [
    "main"
   ],
   "textLength": 390,
   "text": "Firefox supports -moz-none, which is just like none except that it means sub-elements can override the cascade and become selectable again with -moz-user-select: text; As of Firefox 21, none behaves like -moz-none.\nInternet Explorer also supports a so-far-proprietary value, element, in which you can select text inside the element but the selection will stop at the bounds of that element.",
